<Base title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for abhibansal.dev and the personal apps that use Google sign-in.">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">This covers abhibansal.dev and the small personal apps I run under it that use Google sign-in (the Google Cloud project "Abhinav apps").</p>

    <h2>Who these apps are for</h2>
    <p>The apps are personal tools. Only accounts I have allowed can sign in, and in practice that is me. If you are not on the allowlist, signing in shows a "not allowed" message and nothing about you is stored.</p>

    <h2>What Google data is used, and how</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Sign-in:</strong> your email address and basic profile, to check you are on the allowlist. The session is kept in an encrypted cookie; there is no user database.</li>
      <li><strong>Gmail and YouTube (my own account only):</strong> my tools read my own mail and subscriptions to sort them and to keep track of my own correspondence. That data stays on my machine or in my private dashboards.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No Google user data is sold, shared with anyone, used for advertising, or used to train AI models. Message text may be sent to an AI service to classify it on my behalf, and to nothing else.</p>

    <h2>The website</h2>
    <p>Visits to abhibansal.dev are counted with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>, which sets no cookies and collects no personal data.</p>

    <h2>Removing access</h2>
    <p>You can revoke any app's access to your Google account at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. For questions, email <a href="mailto:abhibansal60@gmail.com">abhibansal60@gmail.com</a>.</p>

    <p class="meta">Last updated 1 October 2026.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
